{"name":"Old Money","hex":"#2c5c4f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"old money","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Families that have been wealthy for generations or members of such families.","The monetary system used in the United Kingdom and Ireland before decimalisation in 1971 and consisting of pounds, shillings, pence and farthings."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/old_money"}],"entries":[{"title":"£sd","blocks":[{"text":"£sd is the popular name for the pre-decimal currencies once common throughout Europe. The abbreviation originates from the Latin currency denominations librae, solidi, and denarii. Under this system, there were 12 denarii in a solidus and 20 solidi in a libra. In the countries of the (former) British Empire, these were called pounds, shillings, and pence, with 12 pence in a shilling and 20 shillings in a pound."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Guildhall_Museum_Collection-_Drusilla_Dunford_Money_Table_Sampler_3304.JPG/330px-Guildhall_Museum_Collection-_Drusilla_Dunford_Money_Table_Sampler_3304.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/%C2%A3sd"},{"title":"Old Money (The Simpsons)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Old Money\" is the seventeenth episode of the second season of the American animated television series The Simpsons. It originally aired on Fox in the United States on March 28, 1991."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Old_Money_(The_Simpsons)"},{"title":"Old money","blocks":[{"text":"Old money is a social class of the rich who have been able to maintain their wealth over multiple generations, in contrast with new money whose wealth has been acquired within its own generation. The term often refers to perceived members of the de facto aristocracy in societies that historically lack an officially established aristocratic class."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Old_money"},{"title":"Money","blocks":[{"text":"Money is any item or verifiable record that is generally accepted as payment for goods and services and repayment of debts, such as taxes, in a particular country or socio-economic context. The primary functions which distinguish money are: medium of exchange, a unit of account, a store of value and sometimes, a standard of deferred payment."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Euro_coins_and_banknotes_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Euro_coins_and_banknotes_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Money"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Cash_register_%288058279685%29_%282%29.jpg/500px-Cash_register_%288058279685%29_%282%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Cash_register_%288058279685%29_%282%29.jpg/1280px-Cash_register_%288058279685%29_%282%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Cash_register_%288058279685%29_%282%29.jpg/500px-Cash_register_%288058279685%29_%282%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Old till in Ireland, with \"shortcut\" keys in various £sd denominations (lower numbers) and their \"new pence\" equivalent (upper numbers)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACash_register_(8058279685)_(2).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/TOY_%28FindID_748865%29.jpg/500px-TOY_%28FindID_748865%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/TOY_%28FindID_748865%29.jpg/500px-TOY_%28FindID_748865%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Toy coin, which teaches children the value of a shilling","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATOY_(FindID_748865).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Denier_Charlemagne1.jpg/330px-Denier_Charlemagne1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Denier_Charlemagne1.jpg/330px-Denier_Charlemagne1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Carolingian denarius","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADenier_Charlemagne1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/IBM_1401_Control_Panel.jpg/500px-IBM_1401_Control_Panel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/IBM_1401_Control_Panel.jpg/1280px-IBM_1401_Control_Panel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/IBM_1401_Control_Panel.jpg/500px-IBM_1401_Control_Panel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"1401 Console and, below, the Auxiliary Console.  The grey knob nearest the centre of the Auxiliary Console mentions \"PENCE\" and \"SHILL\".","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIBM_1401_Control_Panel.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Drury_Lane_Notice_Board_VA.jpg/500px-Drury_Lane_Notice_Board_VA.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Drury_Lane_Notice_Board_VA.jpg/1280px-Drury_Lane_Notice_Board_VA.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Drury_Lane_Notice_Board_VA.jpg/500px-Drury_Lane_Notice_Board_VA.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm